  "body_html": "<p>I'm currently reading <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/51860322-science-illustration-a-history-of-visual-knowledge-from-the-15th-centur\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Science Illustration — A History of Visual Knowledge from the 15th Century to Today</a>. Highly recommended! Great books on science and/or design, are always a source of inspiration for me. </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/a5ce2dd2.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/a5ce2dd2.jpg\" alt=\"Science Illustration\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"1147\"></a></p>\n\n<p>The book is a treasure trove of great illustrations — and some of them are just <strong>meant to be coded</strong> in <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>! ... like this one (sorry for the bad quality, picture taken with my phone):</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/c6d08bad.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/c6d08bad.jpg\" alt=\"Interconnecting lines\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"1058\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Luckily, it's not overly complex to do in <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>. </p>\n\n<p>We just need a bit of Math and JavaScript.</p>\n\n<p>To start with, we need a canvas:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight html\"><code><span class=\"nt\">&lt;svg</span> <span class=\"na\">viewBox=</span><span class=\"s\">\"0 0 1000 1000\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Now, we need some data!</p>\n\n<p>The <code>viewBox</code> has a <code>size</code> of 1000, and we need 16 points around the circle:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">size</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">1000</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">radius</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">size</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">numOfPoints</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Next, let's create an array of points:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code>  <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">data</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[...</span><span class=\"k\">new</span> <span class=\"nc\">Array</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">numOfPoints</span><span class=\"p\">)].</span><span class=\"nf\">map</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"nx\">_a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">index</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">angle</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">360</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"nx\">numOfPoints</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">radian</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">angle</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">index</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"nf\">polarToCartesian</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">radian</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">})</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>We need a small helper-method, <code>polarToCartesian</code>, to get the coordinates of our 16 points:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">polarToCartesian</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">degrees</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">radians</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">degrees</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">PI</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"mf\">180.0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">cos</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">radians</span><span class=\"p\">)),</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">sin</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">radians</span><span class=\"p\">))]</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>A method like this typically needs <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> as well, but since these are the same as <code>radius</code> (in this case), we can go for a simpler version.</p>\n\n<p>Cool, now we have an array of arrays:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">961.9397662556433</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">691.3417161825449</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">853.5533905932738</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">853.5533905932737</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">...</span><span class=\"nx\">etc</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>For each point, we need to draw a line to all the other points, feeding in the <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code>of the current point:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">renderLines</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">X</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nx\">Y</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"nx\">data</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">map</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">entry</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"k\">if </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">X</span> <span class=\"o\">!==</span> <span class=\"nx\">x</span> <span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"nx\">Y</span> <span class=\"o\">!==</span> <span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"s2\">`&lt;line x1=\"</span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">X</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\" y1=\"</span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">Y</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\" x2=\"</span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\" y2=\"</span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;&lt;/line&gt;`</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">})</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Now, the only thing remaining is to call that method and set the returned string as <code>innerHTML</code> of our <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"nx\">svg</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">innerHTML</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">data</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">map</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">entry</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"nf\">renderLines</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nf\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"dl\">''</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">})</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Let's see what we've built:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/55606fd9.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/55606fd9.jpg\" alt=\"BW Interconnecting Lines\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"790\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Looks great, but a bit dull! Let's add a method for generating random values between a <code>min</code> and a <code>max</code>-range:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">random</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">max</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">min</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">floor</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">max</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"nx\">min</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"nx\">min</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>... and then use it to create random colors and stroke-widths:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\">\n<pre class=\"highlight javascript\"><code><span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">stroke</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">`hsl(</span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nf\">random</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">360</span><span class=\"p\">)}</span><span class=\"s2\">, </span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nf\">random</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">)}</span><span class=\"s2\">%, </span><span class=\"p\">${</span><span class=\"nf\">random</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">90</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">)}</span><span class=\"s2\">%)`</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span> <span class=\"nx\">strokeWidth</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nf\">random</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\">\n<div class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\">\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"><title>Enter fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n    <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"><title>Exit fullscreen mode</title>\n    <path d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"></path>\n</svg>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/a65614f6.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/a65614f6.jpg\" alt=\"Colour Interconnecting Lines\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"795\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Much better! Let's try to change the <code>numberOfPoints</code>-variable to a much lower value:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/6b9332c3.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/6b9332c3.jpg\" alt=\"Fewer points\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"785\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Or perhaps a much higher value?</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"assets/1185936/4d34058e.jpg\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"assets/1185936/4d34058e.jpg\" alt=\"Many points\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"796\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Wow! Almost like a kaleidoscope. Or a rubber-ball!</p>\n\n<h2>\n  <a name=\"demo\" href=\"#demo\">\n  </a>\n  Demo\n</h2>\n\n<p>I hope this little post inspired you to do some creative things with <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>. </p>\n\n<p>Below is a Pen, where you can drag the \"points\"-slider to in- or decrease the number of points.</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"600\" src=\"https://codepen.io/stoumann/embed/GRdgbjN?height=600&amp;default-tab=result&amp;embed-version=2\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" allowtransparency=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\n</iframe>\n</p>\n\n",
  "body_markdown": "I'm currently reading [Science Illustration — A History of Visual Knowledge from the 15th Century to Today](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/51860322-science-illustration-a-history-of-visual-knowledge-from-the-15th-centur). Highly recommended! Great books on science and/or design, are always a source of inspiration for me. \n\n![Science Illustration](assets/1185936/e9bf8f6d.jpg)\n\nThe book is a treasure trove of great illustrations — and some of them are just **meant to be coded** in `<svg>`! ... like this one (sorry for the bad quality, picture taken with my phone):\n\n![Interconnecting lines](assets/1185936/636a8ad8.jpeg)\n\nLuckily, it's not overly complex to do in `<svg>`. \n\nWe just need a bit of Math and JavaScript.\n\nTo start with, we need a canvas:\n\n```html\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\"></svg>\n```\n\nNow, we need some data!\n\nThe `viewBox` has a `size` of 1000, and we need 16 points around the circle:\n\n```js\nconst size = 1000;\nconst radius = size / 2;\nconst numOfPoints = 16;\n```\n\nNext, let's create an array of points:\n```js\n  const data = [...new Array(numOfPoints)].map((_a, index) => {\n    const angle = 360 / numOfPoints;\n    const radian = angle * (index + 1);\n    return polarToCartesian(radius, radian)\n  })\n```\n\nWe need a small helper-method, `polarToCartesian`, to get the coordinates of our 16 points:\n\n\n```js\nconst polarToCartesian = (r, degrees) => {\n    const radians = degrees * Math.PI / 180.0;\n    return [r + (r * Math.cos(radians)), r + (r * Math.sin(radians))]\n  }\n```\n\nA method like this typically needs `x` and `y` as well, but since these are the same as `radius` (in this case), we can go for a simpler version.\n\nCool, now we have an array of arrays:\n\n```js\n[\n  [961.9397662556433, 691.3417161825449],\n  [853.5533905932738, 853.5533905932737],\n  ...etc,\n]\n```\n\nFor each point, we need to draw a line to all the other points, feeding in the `X` and `Y`of the current point:\n\n```js\nconst renderLines = (X,Y) => {\n    return data.map(entry => {\n      const [x,y] = entry;\n      if (X !== x && Y !== y) return `<line x1=\"${X}\" y1=\"${Y}\" x2=\"${x}\" y2=\"${y}\"></line>`\n    })\n  }\n```\n\nNow, the only thing remaining is to call that method and set the returned string as `innerHTML` of our `<svg>`:\n\n```js\nsvg.innerHTML = data.map(entry => {\n    const [x,y] = entry;\n    return renderLines(x,y).join('');\n  })\n```\n\nLet's see what we've built:\n\n\n![BW Interconnecting Lines](assets/1185936/a60cffe6.png)\n\nLooks great, but a bit dull! Let's add a method for generating random values between a `min` and a `max`-range: \n\n```js\nconst random = (max, min = 0) => Math.floor(Math.random() * (max - min) + min);\n```\n\n... and then use it to create random colors and stroke-widths:\n\n```js\nconst stroke = `hsl(${random(360)}, ${random(100, 50)}%, ${random(90, 30)}%)`;\nconst strokeWidth = random(30, 3) / 10;\n```\n\n![Colour Interconnecting Lines](assets/1185936/1ce1069e.png)\n\nMuch better! Let's try to change the `numberOfPoints`-variable to a much lower value:\n\n\n![Fewer points](assets/1185936/60a32a1b.png)\n\nOr perhaps a much higher value?\n\n\n![Many points](assets/1185936/dfe131ef.png)\n\nWow! Almost like a kaleidoscope. Or a rubber-ball!\n\n## Demo\n\nI hope this little post inspired you to do some creative things with `<svg>`. \n\nBelow is a Pen, where you can drag the \"points\"-slider to in- or decrease the number of points.\n\n\n{% codepen https://codepen.io/stoumann/pen/GRdgbjN %}",
